  "definitions": {
    "R2": "stored entry_date != e, or stored fwd_1d NULL or more than 0.01 away from 100 x (close/open - 1): refused and counted, never scored on the stored value; the remedy is a whole-table compute-performance --all and a new run number",
    "board_hits": "report only: close(e) x adj(e) >= 1.07 x close(t) x adj(t); this one DOES depend on adj_factor because it spans two rows",
    "e": "the first date after t in the market calendar (every date with any daily_prices row); computed from the calendar, never read from the stored entry_date, which is only the R2 cross-check",
    "entry_open_at_limit_proxy": "report only: open(s, e) x 1000 >= close(s, t) x 1095 on raw prices as §2 R3 writes it; an ex-dividend e understates it",
    "event": "the first day of a run of consecutive market days on the list; a market day without the stock on the list breaks the run",
    "hit": "100 x close(s, e) >= 107 x open(s, e) on raw prices of the entry day e, compared in decimal; buy at the next market day's open, mark at its close. The overnight gap is excluded because nobody can buy it",
    "on_list": "verbatim json_export: close on t, stocks.type='stock', final >= 65, sorted by (final, branch_score with None as -inf, turnover) desc, first 40; full ties at the cap are all included",
    "pools": "P_stock: same stock, same half, rows not on the list passing R1 and R2; P_date: same date, other stocks, rows not on the list passing R1 and R2. Days whose next day is a list day are deliberately NOT removed (§3.3)"
  },
